{"type":"assistant","uuid":"4183abee-b19d-4b2f-a0aa-5704dac1da38","session_id":"e6ff3617-b598-4094-bfda-89ba04c86ed5","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"4183abee-b19d-4b2f-a0aa-5704dac1da38","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear understanding of the bug. In `Previewer.java`, the `onCreate()` method reads `mCardList` and `mIndex` directly from the intent:\n\n```java\nmCardList = getIntent().getLongArrayExtra(\"cardList\");\nmIndex = getIntent().getIntExtra(\"index\", -1);\n```\n\nBut it never checks `savedInstanceState` to restore these values after a configuration change (like screen rotation). So every time the screen rotates, the activity is recreated and `mIndex` is reset to whatever the intent provides.\n\nHowever, the intent is recreated from scratch during rotation with the same extras... Actually wait, let me think about this more carefully.\n\n\nWhen the activity is recreated after rotation, `savedInstanceState` is not null, but the code ignores it and always reads fresh values from the intent, which resets `mIndex` to its original starting position instead of restoring the card the user was viewing.\n\nThe fix is to check `savedInstanceState` in `onCreate()` and restore `mCardList` and `mIndex` from the bundle if it exists.\n\nNow I'm realizing there's another issue in `onCollectionLoaded()` where `mCurrentCard` is retrieved using the restored `mIndex` — but I need to make sure the index restoration logic is solid before diving deeper into that flow. Writing the fix...\n\nNow I'm checking the bounds validation in `onCreate()` to see how it handles the restored values. the `savedInstanceState` path:\n\nIf mIndex was 0 (first card), then the user would expect to still be on the first card's question, but displayCardQuestion() is called which would reset mShowingAnswer = false.\n\nActually, wait - after rotation, if the user was looking at the answer of card 5, we want to restore them to card 5's answer. But our current fix only restores to the question because displayCardQuestion() always shows the question.\n\nHmm, but let me re-think this. The user is previewing cards. They navigate through several cards. Then they rotate the screen. The bug is that they go back to the first card. The expected behavior is they should stay on the current card they were viewing.\n\nFor now, the minimal fix is to just restore mCardList and mIndex from savedInstanceState so the user stays on the same card after rotation. Restoring the show/hide state of the answer would require additional changes to mShowingAnswer, but the core issue is preventing the jump back to card 0.\n\nLooking at how similar activities handle this—like CardBrowser—would help me understand the right pattern for preserving the user's position through configuration changes. I need to save `mCardList` and `mIndex` to the bundle in `onSaveInstanceState()`, then restore them in `onCreate()` before reading from the intent. In `onCreate()`, I'll only extract the extras from the intent if `savedInstanceState` is null, otherwise use the saved values. I should also check if `mCardList` could be null when restoring.\n\nI'm considering whether to save `mShowingAnswer` too, but since the user might be viewing the answer or question when rotating, I'll keep the fix minimal for now—just preserving the card position should be enough. I should also verify if `AbstractFlashcardViewer` has a lifecycle method I should override instead.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"1ce3ba7b-0f6c-403d-9584-a7846aa0bc84","session_id":"e6ff3617-b598-4094-bfda-89ba04c86ed5","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"1ce3ba7b-0f6c-403d-9584-a7846aa0bc84","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nNow I understand the bug clearly. In `Previewer.java`:\n\n1. `onCreate()` always reads `mCardList` and `mIndex` from the intent\n2. There's no `onSaveInstanceState()` to save `mIndex`\n3. There's no restoration from `savedInstanceState`\n\nSo when the screen rotates, the activity is recreated and `mIndex` always resets to the original index from the intent (usually 0), causing it to go back to the first card.\n\nLet me apply the fix:\n\n"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
