{"type":"assistant","uuid":"c44188fc-fa17-472e-9235-a9372430c966","session_id":"e6ff3617-b598-4094-bfda-89ba04c86ed5","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"c44188fc-fa17-472e-9235-a9372430c966","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe bug has been fixed. Here's a summary:\n\n## Root Cause\nIn `Previewer.java`, when the Android activity is recreated due to a screen rotation (configuration change), the `onCreate()` method always read `mCardList` and `mIndex` from the incoming `Intent` extras, ignoring any previously viewed card position. This caused the preview to always restart at the original index (typically the first card).\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n**File:** `AnkiDroid/src/main/java/com/ichi2/anki/Previewer.java`\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **Added state persistence keys** — Three constants for saving/ restoring: `KEY_CARD_LIST`, `KEY_INDEX`, `KEY_SHOWING_ANSWER`\n\n2. **Modified `onCreate()`** — Now checks `savedInstanceState`:\n   - If `null` (first launch): reads card list/index from the Intent\n   - If not `null` (recreation after rotation): restores values from the saved instance state\n\n3. **Added `onSaveInstanceState()`** — Saves `mCardList`, `mIndex`, and `mShowingAnswer` to the bundle before the activity is destroyed during rotation\n\n4. **Modified `onCollectionLoaded()`** — Conditionally calls `displayCardAnswer()` or `displayCardQuestion()` based on the restored `mShowingAnswer` state, so if the user was viewing the answer before rotation, the answer is shown after rotation\n\nThe patch file is at: `bug-273/Previewer.patch`"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52085,"output_tokens":337,"cache_read_input_tokens":50304,"total_tokens":52422}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"9faa640f-600d-4835-86d2-0bb2c48dd437","session_id":"e6ff3617-b598-4094-bfda-89ba04c86ed5","is_error":false,"duration_ms":87350,"duration_api_ms":70119,"num_turns":33,"result":"\n\nThe bug has been fixed. Here's a summary:\n\n## Root Cause\nIn `Previewer.java`, when the Android activity is recreated due to a screen rotation (configuration change), the `onCreate()` method always read `mCardList` and `mIndex` from the incoming `Intent` extras, ignoring any previously viewed card position. This caused the preview to always restart at the original index (typically the first card).\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n**File:** `AnkiDroid/src/main/java/com/ichi2/anki/Previewer.java`\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **Added state persistence keys** — Three constants for saving/ restoring: `KEY_CARD_LIST`, `KEY_INDEX`, `KEY_SHOWING_ANSWER`\n\n2. **Modified `onCreate()`** — Now checks `savedInstanceState`:\n   - If `null` (first launch): reads card list/index from the Intent\n   - If not `null` (recreation after rotation): restores values from the saved instance state\n\n3. **Added `onSaveInstanceState()`** — Saves `mCardList`, `mIndex`, and `mShowingAnswer` to the bundle before the activity is destroyed during rotation\n\n4. **Modified `onCollectionLoaded()`** — Conditionally calls `displayCardAnswer()` or `displayCardQuestion()` based on the restored `mShowingAnswer` state, so if the user was viewing the answer before rotation, the answer is shown after rotation\n\nThe patch file is at: `bug-273/Previewer.patch`","usage":{"input_tokens":1294487,"output_tokens":10842,"cache_read_input_tokens":1209392,"total_tokens":1305329},"permission_denials":[]}
